# Troubleshooting a 502 Response

A 502 response from nginx usually means it could not get a valid response from the upstream application.

> [!WARNING]
> Reload nginx only after validating the configuration. An invalid configuration can interrupt traffic.

```nginx
location / {
    proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:3000;
    proxy_set_header Host $host;
}
```

## Checks

- Confirm the application is running and listening on `127.0.0.1:3000`.
- Check the nginx error log for connection failures or upstream timeouts.

After making a change, repeat the [Checks](#checks).